"Speak," the king replies, his posture rigid.

"The Overseer contacted us through the blue crystals back in the bunker," I tell him. "He offered us terms to set up an ambush against your vanguard. We refused."

The king glances to his left. "Albert. Is he speaking truthfully?"

Albert's gaze hardens, his fingers tapping the hilt of his shortsword. "He is lying, my lord. The micro-tremors in his aura give him away. They accepted the machine's terms and intend to strike our flank."

"I have heard enough," the underground king says, stepping back. "Albert. Peter. Keep weapons drawn on them. If any of them twitches toward a spell or a blade, cut them down. I will handle the vanguard."

"Alone, my lord?" Albert asks, his eyes wide.

"I have a theory to test," the king says.

}
